<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Rolling back the darkening of the neighbouring month's days (DESIGN §5). Weekends stay dark:
      we undo the 0290 edit only halfway.

      What went wrong. In 0290 the neighbouring month was lowered after the weekend so they would not
      merge in lightness. Arithmetically right, but not on screen: the calendar window is two
      past weeks + the current + the next, and at the start of a month the neighbouring month takes
      MOST of the grid. Measured on 02.08.2026: 19 cells out of 28, i.e. two thirds of the board
      darkened at once, and the calendar read as a solid grey field. By mid-month
      the share drops to 5/28, but living with this for three weeks every month is not acceptable.

      Why the neighbouring month's fill does NOT need to be the darkest: it has a second
      mark, the dimmed figure (text-secondary instead of text-primary). A weekend carries
      only the fill, so the depth goes to it, while the neighbouring month gets by with the pair
      "quiet fill + quiet figure".

      A consequence accepted deliberately: the weekend (#f0e1d8) and the neighbouring month (#ece0d7)
      became almost equal in lightness. Side by side they are not confused: the neighbouring month is recognised
      by its figure; and within the other month's block weekends are not highlighted anyway, because
      the fill priority puts "other month" above "weekend" (and that did not change).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0300-wave-01-othermonth-back" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#ece0d7"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#e3d1c4"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="0300-wave-02-othermonth-back" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#cbe1f6"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#b6d3ee"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
